            </profile>
            <profile id="da17-6483-1287-07ec" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="b792-78e1-7b03-d4d6" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">An infantry unit can be supplied with a Tortoise Wagon, a form of travelling pavise allowing infantry units to cross the beaten zone of enemy crossbow fire. A Tortoise Wagon can provide an infantry unit of maximum six model frontage with hard cover, to the front of the unit only. A unit with a Tortoise Wagon may only move at a maximum of 6". (Not attached to a unit here; field one per supported infantry unit.) (The Art of War p.44)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="50"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntry>
