  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="14e5-b642-9b8d-d615" name="Warring States (Art of War) - List Notes" publicationId="b792-78e1-7b03-d4d6" hidden="false">
      <description>WARRING STATES (The Art of War, pp.41-46). The generic list plus the Armies of Zhao, Qin, Yan, Chu, Qi, Hann and Wei (state variants on p.45). State variants that change the available special units or the Chariotry &amp; Cavalry cap are enforced; frenzy, drummers, stubborn, heavy armour upgrades and Inspiring Red Banners (hongse de hengfu: before the battle roll a D3 per unit for +1 combat resolution bonuses, +15 pts) are documented only. Warring States generals may be Yang or Yin; Military Strategists may use Ruses (see Three Kingdoms notes; not built). The Battle of Chengpu scenario (p.33) is not built. Percentage limits are by points. "May only have one selected option per 1,000 points" for Special Units is documented only.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Warring States - Generic state]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry and Cavalry: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 33%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  WARRING STATES (no state variant). Characters up to 25%. Chariotry &amp; Cavalry up to 25%. Infantry at least 33%. Special Units up to 25% (two selected options per 1,000 points).
[Warring States - Army of Zhao]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry and Cavalry: up to 33%
  Infantry: at least 33%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  ARMY OF ZHAO. Characters up to 25%. Special Units up to 25% (two selected options per 1,000 points). Infantry at least 33%. Chariotry &amp; Cavalry up to 33%. May have 0-2 Light Cavalry Archers instead of 0-1. May take 0-1 Nomad Cavalry allies as a Special Unit.
[Warring States - Army of Qin]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry and Cavalry: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 33%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  ARMY OF QIN. Characters up to 25%. Special Units up to 25% (two selected options per 1,000 points). Infantry at least 33%. Chariotry &amp; Cavalry up to 25%. Swordsmen may become subject to Frenzy when charges are declared, losing any shields and light armour (not enforced). May have 0-2 Light Cavalry Lancers instead of 0-1. May take 0-1 Nomad Cavalry allies as a Special Unit.
[Warring States - Army of Yan]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry and Cavalry: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 33%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  ARMY OF YAN. Characters up to 25%. Special Units up to 25% (two selected options per 1,000 points). Infantry at least 33%. Chariotry &amp; Cavalry up to 25%. Infantry units may have additional drummers (+5 pts; the unit automatically wins a drawn combat by 1 point). May have an Eastern Shaman (Wu) but may not take a Military Strategist. Infantry units (other than Massed Levy) may be made Stubborn (+3 pts). Drummers and Stubborn are documented only.
[Warring States - Army of Chu]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry and Cavalry: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 33%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  ARMY OF CHU. Characters up to 25%. Special Units up to 25% (two selected options per 1,000 points). Infantry at least 33%. Chariotry &amp; Cavalry up to 25%. May make 0-1 unit of Crossbow into Guards, Drilled with heavy armour (+4 pts) (documented only). May take 0-1 Foot Barbarians allies as a Special Unit. May take an Eastern Shaman (Wu) if a Military Strategist is not taken.
[Warring States - Army of Qi]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry and Cavalry: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 33%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  ARMY OF QI. Characters up to 25%. Special Units up to 25% (two selected options per 1,000 points). Infantry at least 33%. Chariotry &amp; Cavalry up to 25%. May give 0-1 Elite units Noble Swords instead of swords (+1 pt); must be used in Skirmish formation (documented only). May take 0-1 Foot Barbarians allies as a Special Unit. May take 0-1 Eastern Shaman (Wu).
[Warring States - Army of Hann]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry and Cavalry: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 33%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  ARMY OF HANN. Characters up to 25%. Special Units up to 25% (two selected options per 1,000 points). Infantry at least 33%. Chariotry &amp; Cavalry up to 25%. May take 0-1 Repeating Crossbow unit as a Special Unit. May give units Inspiring Red Banners (+15 pts) (documented only). May give 0-1 Halberdier or Spear unit heavy armour (+3 pts) (documented only).
[Warring States - Army of Wei]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Chariotry and Cavalry: up to 33%
  Infantry: at least 33%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  ARMY OF WEI. Characters up to 25%. Special Units up to 25% (two selected options per 1,000 points). Infantry at least 33%. Chariotry &amp; Cavalry up to 33%. May take 0-1 Nomad Cavalry allies as a Special Unit. May give infantry units (other than Massed Levy) heavy armour (+3 pts) (documented only).</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
